# Prose that is allowed to appear in two files. See
# DEVELOPERS.md#1-one-topic-one-place for when an entry here is the right
# answer, which is seldom.
#
# One paragraph per allowance: the files it covers, one per line, then the
# passage. Naming them is what makes it deliberate -- a copy in a file not on
# the list is news whatever those on it agreed -- and an allowance nothing
# matches is reported, so the baseline cannot outlive the repetition it
# recorded. A path line has no space in it; that is what tells the two apart.
#
# Keep it short. A long list is the checker being wrong, not the code.

# The label on `forgetAudio`, `forgetDetector`, `forgetLabelCache` and
# `forgetOutbox`: four one-line JSDoc comments on four instances of one idiom,
# a module-level singleton with a reset only a test calls. It is a label
# rather than an explanation -- there is nothing here that could live in one
# place and be linked from the others, and writing it four different ways
# would say the four exports differ when the whole point is that they do not.
# It runs to exactly twelve words, which is the only reason the checker sees
# it at all. A fifth joins the list below rather than costing four more
# entries.

frontend/src/batch/outbox.ts
frontend/src/scan/confirm.ts
frontend/src/scan/decoder.ts
frontend/src/scan/labelCache.ts
Lets a test start again from nothing. Not used by the app.
